THOUGHT: The NullAway error here is that `bindException.getMessage()` may return null, and calling `toLowerCase()` on it is unsafe. I should store the message in a local variable, check it for null, and only then call `toLowerCase().contains("in use")`. This is a minimal, behavior-preserving change that won’t affect other parts of the project. After editing, I’ll re-run the NullAway-checked compilation to confirm the error count drops from 43 to 42.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/spring-boot && sed -i '83,87c\		ifCausedBy(ex, BindException.class, (bindException) -> {
			// bind exception can be also thrown because an address can'''t be assigned
			String message = bindException.getMessage();
			if (message != null && message.toLowerCase().contains("in use")) {
				action.accept(bindException);
			}
		});' spring-boot-project/spring-boot/src/main/java/org/springframework/boot/web/server/PortInUseException.java && ./gradlew :spring-boot-project:spring-boot:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "PortInUseException.java" new_build_output.log || (grep -n "errors" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5 || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log)
```

